      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EMPRESS ASPEN (4) is the horse to beat after coming back from Saturday company in a BM70 at Eagle Farm, where she was steadied leaving the 400m on heavy ground and still finished fifth. Her previous CL2 second at the Sunny Coast was much stronger, beaten a nose over 2200m, and she returns to a trip where she has already won, with a good record at this track. SIR GOLDALOT (2) rates the main danger. He was only even when sixth over 1800m at Gold Coast last week, but his record at this track and distance is excellent and the 2kg claim helps him return to a proven setup. MICHIFUKU (3) improved to fourth at this track last start after jumping awkwardly, and his track-and-distance record gives him a genuine platform if he sharpens again. SHEDRIVESABENTLEY (7) was better than the sixth reads at Doomben, having begun slowly before being held up and steadied late. Worth another look.",
